Sval: a popup window's system backdrop takes the shape it is given

A see-through window's popover keeps its stem, and the system's backdrop
behind its window fills the stem as it fills the body. Gecko lays that
backdrop over the popup's whole window, which reaches past the shape on
every side. XULPopupElement.setWindowShape hands the shape to the widget
(nsIWidget::SetWindowShape) as rings filled even-odd and as rounded
boxes, and each platform's widget shapes its backdrop with the form it
can take: on macOS 26, glass for each box in a container that joins
them (SvalPopupShape.mm); earlier, the menu material masked to the
rings; on Windows, the window's region. The headless widget keeps
whether it has one, which hasWindowShape reads.

